course: dictionary
lesson: 12517
title: Desalt and the word parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To desalt something means to take the salt out of it. Salt is the white powder we sprinkle on chips, and seawater is full of it. When seawater is desalted, the salt is removed, and the water becomes safe to drink.
explain: Look at the word parts to help you. The prefix de- often means remove or take away, as in defrost, which takes away the frost. So desalt means take the salt away. The same idea is in desalination, the process of removing salt.
explain: «The crew used a machine to desalt the seawater, so they had fresh water to drink.» The clue is seawater, which is salty, and the result is fresh drinking water. «Mum soaked the salty ham in water to desalt it.» Soaking takes some of the salt out, so the ham tastes less salty.
fact: To desalt means to remove salt from something.
fact: Desalination is the process of turning seawater into drinking water.
fact: Desalination is important in dry countries, such as parts of Australia and the Middle East, where fresh water is hard to find.
fact: Cooks can desalt salted fish or ham by soaking it in water.
fact: The prefix de- often means remove or take away, which helps you work out words like desalt.
exercise: What does desalt mean? | *To remove salt from something | To make something very hot | To freeze something solid | To add more salt to something
exercise: «The crew used a machine to desalt the seawater.» What did they remove from the seawater? | *Salt | Sand | Oil | Fish
exercise: Which prefix in desalt means remove or take away? | *de- | pre- | sub- | re-
test: «Mum soaked the salty ham in water to desalt it.» Why did Mum soak the ham? | To make it sweeter | *To take some of the salt out | To make it colder | To dry it out
test: Desalination turns seawater into what? | Sea sand | Salty water for cooking | *Drinking water | Ice for drinks
exam: Which sentence uses desalt correctly? | Mum will desalt the ham by adding more salt to it | Mum will desalt the ham by freezing it solid | *Mum will desalt the ham by soaking it in water to take out the salt | Mum will desalt the ham by sprinkling sugar on it
